{
  "name": "FluxFilm · 05 Social auto-post from What's new",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📣 FluxFilm social auto-post — SETUP\nWhen a **What's new** post goes live, the shop calls this workflow (`post.published`). n8n checks the **signature**, then posts the picture + caption + link to your **Telegram channel**. Instagram and Facebook nodes are included but **disabled**.\n\n1. Open **Webhook: post.published** → copy the *Production URL*. In admin → 🔗 Integrations paste it WITHOUT the last part `/post-published` (e.g. `https://you.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/fluxfilm`) → Save, then **Create signing secret** and copy it.\n2. Paste the secret into **Expected signature** → Secret (replace `PASTE_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET`).\n3. Credentials: `Telegram FluxFilm bot` (make the bot an admin of your channel). In **Telegram channel post** set Chat ID to `@yourchannel`.\n4. **Active** on, then publish a post in admin (or press 📡 Send test webhook — the test goes to `/test-ping`, not here).\n\n**Instagram** (disabled): needs an Instagram Business/Creator account linked to a Facebook Page and a long-lived token — steps in docs/n8n/README.md. Only JPEG pictures work.\n**WhatsApp Channels have no API** — post there by hand.\nNo webhooks? Disable the webhook path and enable **Every hour (disabled)** → it polls GET /n8n/api/posts/new.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a22e497e-6fbe-40cf-a6b8-d0793dcd5bda",
      "name": "Setup: social auto-post",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "fluxfilm/post-published",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f738969f-56a5-407a-a1a0-7cae6d470982",
      "name": "Webhook: post.published",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "48a0f6fc-6aec-4348-a2c8-cb5b85d2242f"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "action": "hmac",
        "type": "SHA256",
        "value": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.body) }}",
        "dataPropertyName": "expectedSignature",
        "secret": "PASTE_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET",
        "encoding": "hex"
      },
      "id": "a1632713-f0a0-47c2-a837-fdf8e15161c9",
      "name": "Expected signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.crypto",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "8bf2fc73-4878-438a-a6bc-9273f9b5020c",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-ff-signature'] }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ 'sha256=' + $json.expectedSignature }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "f466b8aa-13fa-4cc4-a42c-4f32df355b8e",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.event }}",
              "rightValue": "post.published",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "7dd63b51-be3c-4191-a9c3-ccb5cdc3b997",
              "leftValue": "={{ Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number($json.headers['x-ff-timestamp'] || 0)) }}",
              "rightValue": 600,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "lt"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "71947ae7-c9f7-4b16-acee-992fc6907d3c",
      "name": "Signature OK and fresh?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((i) => ({ json: i.json.body.data }));"
      },
      "id": "84dec5c5-a18d-406c-a93b-f88c319ac860",
      "name": "Post data (webhook)",
